<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenian port shares fall on first trading day.</title>
<headline>Slovenian port shares fall on first trading day.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Slovenia's sole port, Luka Koper, fell on the first day of trading on the Ljubljana bourse first section.</p>
<p>At 1004 GMT, Luka stood at 2,311 tolars, down from its opening price of 2,600. It was the market's most active stock, though business was choppy with 40,500 shares traded so far. The bourse's second most active stock, Kovinotehna, had traded just 1,100 lots.</p>
<p>But traders said that although foreign interest in Luka Koper was high, the government -- which owns 51 percent -- had still to decide whether foreigners could buy the stock.</p>
</text>
